 ```bash
 herdr server
+herdr server start
 herdr server stop
 herdr server reload-config
 herdr server agent-manifests [--json]
@@ -91,7 +93,7 @@ herdr server update-agent-manifests [--json]
 herdr server reload-agent-manifests
 ```
 
-`herdr server` runs the headless server explicitly. Use it for supervised or service-style setups. `reload-config` applies reloadable settings without restarting panes. `agent-manifests` shows the active agent detection manifest sources, cached remote versions, and last remote update results. `update-agent-manifests` fetches remote manifest updates immediately, reloads them into the running server, and prints the updated manifest status; pass `--json` for the raw status response. `reload-agent-manifests` reloads agent detection manifests into the running server after local override edits.
+`herdr server` runs the headless server explicitly. Use it for supervised or service-style setups. `herdr server start` starts the persistent background server if needed and returns after it is ready. `reload-config` applies reloadable settings without restarting panes. `agent-manifests` shows the active agent detection manifest sources, cached remote versions, and last remote update results. `update-agent-manifests` fetches remote manifest updates immediately, reloads them into the running server, and prints the updated manifest status; pass `--json` for the raw status response. `reload-agent-manifests` reloads agent detection manifests into the running server after local override edits.
 
